# Answers to the newbie questions above (0.36-se.4: before, they got "hm" or a camp tip).
@kind reply
@who *
@answers ask_xpneeded
watch the xp bar, every bubble is a tenth of a level
ten bubbles on the bar and you ding
the xp bar fills up, a full bar is a level
@answers ask_con
grey gives no xp, green a little, blue and yellow are best
yellow is your level, orange and red hurt, purple means run
blue means a bit easier than you, thats the sweet spot solo
@answers ask_bind
release when you die and you wake up at your bind point
there is no recall, either release or walk back
bind at a bindstone in town, type /bind standing next to it
take a horse from the stablemaster, saves the walk
@answers ask_realmability
special skills you buy at your trainer with realm points
you earn realm points killing enemies in the frontier, then spend them at the trainer
stuff like more health or faster casting, paid for with realm points
dont worry about it yet, they come from rvr
@answers ask_train
you get spec points every level, spend them at your trainer
you can save points up, but visit the trainer often
yes, go see your trainer when you ding, points add up fast
you dont have to, but unspent points do nothing for you
@answers ask_camps
ask around, someone always knows a spot
look for monsters that con blue or yellow and settle in
follow other people, wherever they hunt is a camp
the roads out of town lead to most of them, just explore a bit
@answers ask_campshare
ask first, most people will share
not without asking, thats rude
ask in /say, if they say no find another spot
fine if you ask and dont steal their pulls
@answers ask_bags
sell the junk to any merchant, keep only upgrades
keep quest items and gear upgrades, sell the rest
anything good, try the exchange, the rest goes to a merchant
drop the grey loot, it adds up fast
@answers ask_guards
guards attack monsters near them, run to them when in trouble
thats their job, free help when you are dying
lead the bad pulls to the guards, they sort it out
they protect the town, monsters that follow you in get killed
@answers ask_lfg
looking for group
lfg means looking for group, lfm means looking for more
it means looking for group, say it with your level and class
looking for group. if someone says it, they want a group
@answers ask_guild
ask someone with a guild tag, an officer can invite you
watch faction, guilds recruit there all the time
find a guild you like and send them a tell
an officer types /gc invite and you accept, easy
@answers ask_safezone
not here, enemies only show up in the frontier
no, they cant get into our home zones
you are safe here, the fighting is in the frontier and battlegrounds
nope, only in rvr zones, relax and level

@kind ambient
@topic veteran
@who *
@levels 40-50
tip for new folks: train your skills every level, it adds up
dont rush, the 20s are where you learn your class
consider before you pull, it saves a lot of deaths
camp bonus is real, find a quiet spot and stay
group when you can, solo when you must
keep a few potions handy, thank me later
spec for what you enjoy, not what the forums say
your bind point is a lifesaver, set it near your camp
a good healer is worth more than any drop
if a group wipes, laugh, regroup, try again
the frontier is a different game, go when you are ready
crafters are your friends, be nice to them

